  "synthesis": {
    "description": "Ahead of each month, the contract administrator for Houston Pipe Line compiles a report of contract assignments, terminations, expirations and contracts still in process, and mails it as an attachment to schedulers, traders and logistics staff, who read it for changes affecting their deals. A later round is a dated status snapshot sent near month end. When a month's report is missed, the sender owns up and catches up in the next mailing.",
    "steps": [
      "Pull the contract changes for the coming month from the contract system.",
      "Sort them into assignments, terminations, expirations and contracts in process.",
      "Build the report spreadsheet and date it with the as-of time.",
      "Mail the report as an attachment to the distribution of schedulers and logistics staff.",
      "Recipients check the report for contracts that affect their nominations and deals."
    ],
    "approach": "Generate the assignment, termination and expiration report directly from the contract system on a fixed schedule, with a calendar reminder and a send checklist so no month is skipped, and a standard cover note naming the period and as-of time.",
    "rationale": "The report is the same layout every month and the one failure the mail shows is a skipped month, which a dated monthly checklist covering pull, sort, build and send prevents most directly.",
    "artifact_type": "checklist"
  },
  "formula": {
